# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-arms what each hand held, out of the backpack, when a cast or a disarm empties it.
# Hands are recorded at Play, before recovery can cast, then every two seconds. An empty
# remembered hand is seen on every pass, and the weapon is asked back once that hand has
# been empty for interval__rearm_settle, past the cast that emptied it and its cursor.
# Each layer keeps its serial across Plays. A missing item is forgotten, and a replacement
# seen on that layer takes over. No label or weapon table is needed.
# With rearm_follow_hands 1, a new held item adopts both current hands, so an old item on
# the other layer cannot replace a manually chosen weapon. Empty hands retain memory.
# With no remembered item, rearm_graphic picks from the backpack. Its pending serial
# stays fixed until a hand confirms it or it leaves the backpack. The first request
# uses lefthand, as hotkey/weapon-katana does. The actual layer is read after the equip.
# An equip request is not proof of success. In-game checks: Open items part 16.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ config
#
#   config__rearm_graphic
#      Graphic of the weapon to pick out of the backpack while both hands are empty and
#      nothing is remembered. 0 disables that search. A chosen serial is retried until
#      a hand confirms it or it leaves the backpack. Graphics: content/public/game/item-list.md.
#
#   config__rearm_follow_hands
#      What to remember when equipment changes.
#        0  remember each hand independently
#        1  adopt both current hands at Play and when a new held item is seen. Forget an
#           empty opposite hand in that case. If both hands are empty, keep the memory
#           so a cast or disarm can still be repaired
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__rearm_graphic 0
@setvar! config__rearm_follow_hands 0


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ wait
#
#   interval__equip_retry
#      How often the hands are read in full, and how long one equip request is given
#      before the next. A refused equip, after a disarm for example, waits this long.
#
#   interval__rearm_settle
#      How long a remembered hand must have been empty before its equip goes out. A cast
#      empties the hands as it starts, and its cursor is answered only after casting
#      clears. An equip in that gap replaces the cursor and the spell is lost (Magery
#      part 2), so this outlasts the longest cast of the loops that rearm, Magic
#      Reflection at 1.5 seconds, and its cursor.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! interval__equip_retry 2000
@setvar! interval__rearm_settle 2000


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ timer
#
#   timer__equip
#      Runs from the last full read of the hands.
#
#   timer__equip_sent
#      Runs from the last equip request. Ready on the first pass.
#
#   timer__rearm_missing
#      Runs from the last pass that saw every remembered hand filled. Ready on the first
#      pass.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
timer__equip interval__equip_retry
timer__equip_sent interval__equip_retry
timer__rearm_missing interval__rearm_settle


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ state
#
#   var__rearm_left, var__rearm_right
#      The serial last seen on the two-handed layer (lefthand) and on the one-handed layer
#      (righthand), kept across Stop and Play. 0 means nothing seen yet, or the item gone
#      from hand and backpack.
#
#   var__rearm_pending
#      Backpack choice awaiting a hand observation, not a confirmed equip. Cleared on
#      Play, when an item is seen in hand, or when this choice leaves the backpack.
#
#   var__rearm_sent
#      Scratch: 1 once this check sent an equip, so the second hand waits for the next.
#
#   var__rearm_due
#      Scratch: 1 on a pass that reads the hands, on the clock or because a remembered
#      hand is empty.
#
#   var__rearm_missing
#      Scratch: 1 on a pass that finds a remembered hand empty.
#
#   var__rearm_settling
#      1 once the held equip was logged for this empty spell, so the Journal gets one
#      line. Cleared when the hands are filled.
#
#   var__rearm_seen_left, var__rearm_seen_right
#      Scratch: both current hand serials, read before any equip request. 0 means empty.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
if not varexist var__rearm_left
    @setvar! var__rearm_left 0
endif

if not varexist var__rearm_right
    @setvar! var__rearm_right 0
endif

@setvar! var__rearm_pending 0
@setvar! var__rearm_sent 0
@setvar! var__rearm_due 0
@setvar! var__rearm_missing 0
@setvar! var__rearm_settling 0
@setvar! var__rearm_seen_left 0
@setvar! var__rearm_seen_right 0


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ setup
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Snapshot before the first recovery pass. With follow_hands, visible equipment replaces
# the previous pair. Starting with both hands empty retains the pair for recovery.
if config__rearm_follow_hands = 1
    if not lhandempty or not rhandempty
        @setvar! var__rearm_left 0
        @setvar! var__rearm_right 0
    endif
endif

if findlayer self lefthand as alias__rearm_left
    @setvar! var__rearm_left alias__rearm_left

    if config__sysmsg = 1
        sysmsg "Rearm: two-handed layer remembered, serial={{alias__rearm_left}}." 88
    endif
endif

if findlayer self righthand as alias__rearm_right
    @setvar! var__rearm_right alias__rearm_right

    if config__sysmsg = 1
        sysmsg "Rearm: one-handed layer remembered, serial={{alias__rearm_right}}." 88
    endif
endif


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ loop
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # REARM
    #
    # A remembered hand found empty is re-armed once it has been empty for
    # interval__rearm_settle: a cast drops the weapon as it starts, and lhandempty and
    # rhandempty are cheap enough to read every pass. Arming before a cast completes
    # interrupts the cast (wiki Combat Overview), so casting, a cursor, the item queue and
    # hiding block this. casting clears before the cursor is answered, and an equip in that
    # gap loses the spell (Magery part 2, in game 2026-11-01), so the equip also waits
    # until the hand has been empty for interval__rearm_settle. The hold is logged once per
    # empty spell. Every interval__equip_retry both hands are read before an equip: an item
    # in hand is remembered by serial, and a remembered item in neither place is forgotten.
    # With rearm_follow_hands, a new item adopts this pair and forgets an empty opposite
    # hand. Recheck the input guards after finding the packed item, just before lifting it.
    # One equip per pass, the two-handed layer first. The request is not proof of the
    # equip, so the next one waits interval__equip_retry and the hands are read again. With
    # both hands empty and nothing remembered, rearm_graphic names the one to pick.
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    @setvar! var__rearm_due 0
    @setvar! var__rearm_missing 0

    if var__rearm_left != 0 and lhandempty
        @setvar! var__rearm_missing 1
    elseif var__rearm_right != 0 and rhandempty
        @setvar! var__rearm_missing 1
    endif

    if var__rearm_missing = 0
        settimer "timer__rearm_missing" 0
        @setvar! var__rearm_settling 0
    endif

    if timer "timer__equip" >= interval__equip_retry
        @setvar! var__rearm_due 1
    elseif var__rearm_missing = 1
        @setvar! var__rearm_due 1
    endif

    if var__rearm_due = 1
        if not hidden and not queued and not casting and not targetexists
            settimer "timer__equip" 0
            @setvar! var__rearm_sent 0
            @setvar! var__rearm_seen_left 0
            @setvar! var__rearm_seen_right 0

            if findlayer self lefthand as alias__rearm_left
                @setvar! var__rearm_seen_left alias__rearm_left
            endif

            if findlayer self righthand as alias__rearm_right
                @setvar! var__rearm_seen_right alias__rearm_right
            endif

            if config__rearm_follow_hands = 1
                if var__rearm_seen_left != 0 and var__rearm_seen_left != var__rearm_left
                    @setvar! var__rearm_left 0
                    @setvar! var__rearm_right 0
                elseif var__rearm_seen_right != 0 and var__rearm_seen_right != var__rearm_right
                    @setvar! var__rearm_left 0
                    @setvar! var__rearm_right 0
                endif
            endif

            if var__rearm_seen_left != 0
                @setvar! var__rearm_pending 0

                if var__rearm_left != var__rearm_seen_left
                    @setvar! var__rearm_left var__rearm_seen_left

                    if config__sysmsg = 1
                        sysmsg "Rearm: two-handed layer remembered, serial={{var__rearm_left}}." 88
                    endif
                endif
            endif

            if var__rearm_seen_right != 0
                @setvar! var__rearm_pending 0

                if var__rearm_right != var__rearm_seen_right
                    @setvar! var__rearm_right var__rearm_seen_right

                    if config__sysmsg = 1
                        sysmsg "Rearm: one-handed layer remembered, serial={{var__rearm_right}}." 88
                    endif
                endif
            endif

            if var__rearm_seen_left = 0 and var__rearm_left != 0 and timer "timer__equip_sent" >= interval__equip_retry
                if timer "timer__rearm_missing" >= interval__rearm_settle
                    if find var__rearm_left backpack as alias__rearm_packed
                        if not hidden and not queued and not casting and not targetexists
                            # lift waits for the held item. The sent timer spaces the next request,
                            # so a refused equip after a disarm does not stall recovery.
                            lift alias__rearm_packed
                            drop self lefthand
                            @setvar! var__rearm_sent 1
                            settimer "timer__equip_sent" 0

                            if config__sysmsg = 1
                                sysmsg "Rearm: equip requested on the two-handed layer, serial={{alias__rearm_packed}}. The next check reads the hands." 88
                            endif

                            wait wait__short
                        endif
                    else
                        @setvar! var__rearm_left 0
                    endif
                elseif var__rearm_settling = 0 and config__sysmsg = 1
                    sysmsg "Rearm: hand empty for under {{interval__rearm_settle}} ms, equip held." 88
                    @setvar! var__rearm_settling 1
                endif
            endif

            if var__rearm_sent = 0 and var__rearm_seen_right = 0 and var__rearm_right != 0 and timer "timer__equip_sent" >= interval__equip_retry
                if timer "timer__rearm_missing" >= interval__rearm_settle
                    if find var__rearm_right backpack as alias__rearm_packed
                        if not hidden and not queued and not casting and not targetexists
                            lift alias__rearm_packed
                            drop self righthand
                            @setvar! var__rearm_sent 1
                            settimer "timer__equip_sent" 0

                            if config__sysmsg = 1
                                sysmsg "Rearm: equip requested on the one-handed layer, serial={{alias__rearm_packed}}. The next check reads the hands." 88
                            endif

                            wait wait__short
                        endif
                    else
                        @setvar! var__rearm_right 0
                    endif
                elseif var__rearm_settling = 0 and config__sysmsg = 1
                    sysmsg "Rearm: hand empty for under {{interval__rearm_settle}} ms, equip held." 88
                    @setvar! var__rearm_settling 1
                endif
            endif

            if var__rearm_sent = 0 and config__rearm_graphic != 0 and var__rearm_left = 0 and var__rearm_right = 0 and lhandempty and rhandempty and timer "timer__equip_sent" >= interval__equip_retry
                if not find var__rearm_pending backpack
                    @setvar! var__rearm_pending 0

                    if findtype config__rearm_graphic backpack as alias__rearm_pick
                        @setvar! var__rearm_pending alias__rearm_pick
                    endif
                endif

                if find var__rearm_pending backpack as alias__rearm_found
                    if not hidden and not queued and not casting and not targetexists
                        # Keep the choice separate from the confirmed hand serials.
                        lift alias__rearm_found
                        drop self lefthand
                        settimer "timer__equip_sent" 0

                        if config__sysmsg = 1
                            sysmsg "Rearm: graphic {{config__rearm_graphic}} picked from the backpack, serial={{alias__rearm_found}}. The next check reads the hands." 88
                        endif

                        wait wait__short
                    endif
                elseif timer "timer__message" >= interval__message
                    overhead "[ weapon, out ]" 254
                    settimer "timer__message" 0
                endif
            endif
        endif
    endif
